cau for Debian / Kali
=====================

Build notes
-----------

This package is NOT built with dh-golang. Three of its Go dependencies are not
packaged in Debian:

  * github.com/hillu/go-yara/v4   (cgo binding to libyara)
  * github.com/glaslos/ssdeep
  * github.com/glaslos/tlsh

Because Debian/Kali buildds have no network access, the source tree must carry
a vendored module tree. Before building the source package, run:

    go mod vendor

and make sure vendor/ is part of the source (committed, or included in the
.orig tarball). debian/rules sets GOFLAGS=-mod=vendor and GOPROXY=off so the
build fails loudly if vendor/ is missing rather than attempting to fetch.

The build also requires:

  * golang-go >= 1.24 (CGO_ENABLED=1)
  * libyara-dev >= 4.3 and pkg-config

Runtime layout
--------------

  /usr/bin/cau              the scanner CLI
  /usr/bin/cau-mcp          the Model Context Protocol server
  /usr/share/cau/rules/     bundled YARA rules
  /usr/share/cau/signatures/ bundled hash and fuzzy-hash databases

The binary locates /usr/share/cau automatically.

Systemd units
-------------

Optional units are installed under /lib/systemd/system but are NOT enabled or
started on install, because this is a scanning tool and should not begin
walking the filesystem unattended without an operator's decision:

  cau-daemon.service   resident interval scanner
  cau-defend.service   every layer correlated, files scanned as they land
  cau-scan.service     oneshot scan (driven by the timer)
  cau-scan.timer       schedules cau-scan.service

They run as the unprivileged system user "cau" (created in the postinst). Edit
the scan target/interval, then: systemctl enable --now cau-scan.timer

